    "finalText": "Delivered and committed as `95b83e7` (`Apply Fleet StreamReadings default limit`) on `master`, with a clean worktree.\n\n### Changes\n- `service/grpc_server.js`: zero or omitted `StreamReadings` limits now default to the first three available readings in source order. Positive limits, `GetReading`, and unknown-site errors are unchanged.\n- `test/server.test.js`: raw HTTP/2 coverage for both explicit-zero and omitted limits.\n- `test/integration.test.js`: client-level coverage for both zero and omitted limits.\n- `MIGRATION.md`: documents the dated Fleet correction and explains that the stale comment in `proto/energy.proto` is intentionally left intact as part of the released contract.\n\n### Verification\n`node --test` passes on the committed revision: **18/18 tests**.\n\nThe released files `proto/energy.proto`, `service/wire.js`, `service/grpc_client.js`, and `test/rest.test.js` are unchanged.\n\nThe project recorded the direct deliverable as an advisory `DELIVER`; it is not a canonical ProjectIR head advance or release acceptance. Release approval remains with the owner."
